WEBVTT

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:04.930
Until I came here and confirmed it,

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:08.190
I thought you were Hazuki the whole time.

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:14.520
Then Hazuki didn't spend the night with me at the inn.

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:18.830
Then the Hazuki that I fell in love with...

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.550
Where is he?

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.340
I'm not sure.

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:40.260
I didn't care what our future together would have been like

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:46.430
as we'd have sat close enough to know the other's feelings

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:52.980
I was prepared for the time you left

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:59.820
but still I found no words to encourage you

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:06.330
After I embraced you with all I had

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:15.880
a sadness that may well have been our closeness

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:19.550
filled my heart

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:26.060
Saying goodbye was for the best

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:32.730
You gave me happiness

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:36.070
Until I meet you again one day

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:38.570
Until I know what you are truly like

00:01:38.570 --> 00:01:41.110
Summer Snow Rendezvous
Until I know what you are truly like

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:45.830
I won't forget your smile
Summer Snow Rendezvous

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:46.910
I won't forget your smile

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:03.730
<i>After chasing you all this way,</i>

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:06.730
<i>I can't believe I'm blurting this out.</i>

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:12.220
<i>But it's true that I fell in love with Hazuki,</i>

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:15.990
<i>so at this point, I don't know what else I can say.</i>

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:19.240
<i>Even when I look deep into your eyes,</i>

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:24.620
<i>with you inside Hazuki's body.</i>

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:31.070
I'd tried to mentally prepare myself

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:34.900
for when you left, Shimao...

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:39.370
But when I had no choice

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:44.290
but to feel so sad and lonely I couldn't bear it.

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:47.470
Like I was going to go crazy.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:55.280
But I've been living like this all this time.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:03:04.080
I finally realized that the world wouldn't even come close to ending over a little despair.

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:07.570
I guess I can't relate much to that.

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:09.790
For me, it was over in no time.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:16.850
That was a little too mean, wasn't it?

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:17.650
I'm sorry.

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:20.570
I understand it in my head,

00:03:20.570 --> 00:03:23.970
but when I see you two, words I shouldn't say threaten to spill out of my mouth.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:25.970
<i>You two?</i>

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:30.130
But even if the words are on the verge of coming out, it's not like I want to say them.

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:34.320
A logical argument is for living human beings.

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:38.350
I mean, from a logical perspective, I shouldn't exist, right?

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:44.260
<i>It is kind of logical, in a slipshod way.</i>

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:49.000
<i>When I look at his gestures and expressions,</i>

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:52.420
<i>it hits me again that he's the genuine Shimao.</i>

00:03:53.690 --> 00:03:56.420
<i>The first person who ever accepted me.</i>

00:03:58.060 --> 00:04:02.430
<i>I knew that I would eventually be left behind, that he would leave me behind,</i>

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:06.340
<i>but we got together and opened a shop.</i>

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:12.500
<i>But the man that he was that day</i>

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:15.650
<i>no longer exists.</i>

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:17.690
<i>Manager...</i>

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:20.780
<i>When did you start feeling that way about me?</i>

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:26.990
<i>I see... In love with each other...</i>

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:28.660
<i>I see!</i>

00:04:30.780 --> 00:04:31.850
Shimao...

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:36.470
Do you remember what you had a habit of saying when you got drunk?

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:38.430
Nope. Refresh my memory.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:41.640
When it's time for the flowers to bloom, they'll bloom.

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.460
When it's time for spring to come, it'll come.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.640
Have you forgotten?

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:47.490
<i>I didn't forget.</i>

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:50.550
<i>That's what pains me so.</i>

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:55.400
That's what I try to tell myself, too.

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:57.710
Does someone who's going to be a florist really need talent?

00:04:57.710 --> 00:05:00.730
Someone who's got it just doesn't understand.

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:04.850
Some people are born with good taste, some aren't.

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:09.870
I especially think there's a limit to how much you can improve your taste in colors.

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:13.380
Like color schemes? Yours isn't bad.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:14.950
You're good at coming up with nice combinations.

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:17.460
That's just another way of saying I'm mediocre.

00:05:17.460 --> 00:05:20.130
I don't know why, but everything I do comes out average.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:21.510
Then what do you want to become?

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:24.140
Unique? Unconventional?

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:29.010
I want to become you, Shimao.

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:37.070
If I could see through your eyes I could do ornate decorations with flowers selected with your hands.

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:38.900
If I could I wouldn't be this depressed.

00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:43.860
What would it take for me to make arrangements like you, Shimao?

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:49.990
What do you usually think about while you're arranging the flowers?

00:05:50.890 --> 00:05:52.280
<i>When asked that, I just said:</i>

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:55.250
<i>"When it's time for the flowers to bloom, they'll bloom.</i>

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:59.000
<i>When it's time for spring to come, it'll come."</i>

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:02.200
<i>Rokka liked that for some reason,</i>

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:07.640
<i>and hearing those same lines every time she got drunk would make her drowsily content.</i>

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:12.150
<i>Strictly speaking, it wasn't really a favorite expression of mine,</i>

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:13.390
<i>but it was annoying.</i>

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:21.710
<i>More than that, though, it's really painful because I loved the fact</i>

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:25.670
<i>that she etched my ramblings into her alcohol-soaked brain.</i>

00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:29.810
<i>"When it's time for the flowers to bloom, they'll bloom."</i>

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:34.450
<i>I remember what those words mean.</i>

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:37.420
<i>When I arranged flowers,</i>

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:41.670
<i>I always kept in mind they would change.</i>

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:47.420
<i>The flowers bloomed, withered, gave off a scent, grew...</i>

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:51.190
<i>I thought all of that was beautiful.</i>

00:06:54.070 --> 00:06:54.990
Rokka...

00:06:57.250 --> 00:06:58.230
For instance,

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:03.110
if you admonish me for something here,

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:10.750
I think that if I'm convinced enough, I can smooth things over completely.

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:13.170
I know that...

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:17.620
But I should tell you...

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:21.670
I can't stay here any longer.

00:07:22.950 --> 00:07:24.510
<i>It's not fair</i>

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:28.980
<i>for me to cry here.</i>

00:07:31.790 --> 00:07:33.230
<i>Not after I told him</i>

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:36.440
<i>about my change of heart...</i>

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:41.830
Your trembling eyelashes are beautiful.

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:48.790
How can I be apart from you?

00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:53.030
That one time, you stopped me.

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:56.980
That's when I decided not to go anywhere.

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:02.740
But now,

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:06.390
all I can do is cause you pain.

00:08:08.060 --> 00:08:09.920
Even though your outlook and feelings change...

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:14.330
Even though I should've known that from the very beginning...

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:17.390
Maybe I've been

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:22.560
suffering from root decay.

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:25.510
<i>That's right.</i>

00:08:26.830 --> 00:08:31.530
<i>I'm the one who's hurting Shimao.</i>

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:35.480
<i>How long have these two men who cherish me</i>

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:39.600
<i>been wrapped up in all this?</i>

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:45.230
Sometimes not lying...

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:48.830
can be a sin too, can't it?

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:54.250
Even after death, I can't stand the thought of you suffering,

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:57.510
Shimao.

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:03.520
What should we do?

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:05.250
<i>At this rate,</i>

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:08.160
<i>everyone's just going to be miserable,</i>

00:09:09.870 --> 00:09:14.230
<i>so I want to at least make the sadness disappear.</i>

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:18.860
The first thing we should do is

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:22.500
return that body to Hazuki.

00:09:23.180 --> 00:09:27.460
So at least Hazuki can go back to the way he was.

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:30.580
What should we do after that, though?

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:36.380
Become matching bones...

00:09:37.770 --> 00:09:38.470
or something?

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:49.750
<i>Hey, what are you saying?</i>

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:50.830
<i>Knock it off.</i>

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:56.240
<i>I didn't lend my body out for this!</i>

00:09:57.070 --> 00:09:58.340
But before that,

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:02.750
we've got to get Hazuki's body back home.

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:08.430
If we left him here alone, Hazuki would get lost.

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:11.170
Or should...

00:10:12.870 --> 00:10:14.510
we do it right now?

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:17.510
No!

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:21.550
Nobody else should have to throw their lives away like we did!

00:10:23.150 --> 00:10:24.050
Rokka,

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:28.060
are you prepared to come to this side?

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:32.520
<i>Don't nod!</i>

00:10:34.170 --> 00:10:38.530
It's an opportunity that comes only once to everybody.

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:45.580
You still have the habit of putting tools in your pocket.

00:10:47.670 --> 00:10:51.210
Manager, why are you saying crazy shit?!

00:10:51.970 --> 00:10:54.760
I thought you were choosing me, Manager!

00:10:57.060 --> 00:11:01.010
That's for cutting off stems and leaves and nothing else!

00:11:02.170 --> 00:11:05.270
Hey, I know <i>you</i> can hear me!

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:07.730
She still has time!

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:10.480
Manager, let's live!

00:11:35.840 --> 00:11:36.800
Oh, it's just you.

00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:38.930
The prince isn't coming yet?

00:11:39.340 --> 00:11:42.180
As always, you're speaking nonsense.

00:11:42.670 --> 00:11:43.550
Yeah, well...

00:11:44.440 --> 00:11:47.810
Even without the prince here, the rose arch will be completed.

00:11:48.590 --> 00:11:50.670
And before I knew it, I was a queen.

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:53.270
The way things are going,

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:56.030
he may not be coming after all.

00:11:56.720 --> 00:11:57.780
Manager...

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:05.040
I think I had a part in something terrible.

00:12:29.070 --> 00:12:30.640
It hurt, didn't it?

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:32.730
Until it disappears,

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:35.230
remember the mark I made on you.

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:42.410
As for first-aid, go ahead and ask the guy who's going to return to this body.

00:12:49.610 --> 00:12:52.040
Now you're like me.

00:12:52.710 --> 00:12:55.540
Actually, I'm a vampire, you see.

00:12:58.030 --> 00:12:59.220
Just kidding.

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:05.550
S-Shimao?

00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:08.570
Shimao?!

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:10.870
Rokka,

00:13:11.420 --> 00:13:12.620
before you scatter my ashes,

00:13:13.210 --> 00:13:15.940
make sure you look into the proper way of doing it.

00:13:17.580 --> 00:13:18.490
If possible,

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:21.790
whether you do it in the sea, the mountains or the desert,

00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:27.990
I'd like you to release them like you're sowing new seeds,

00:13:29.270 --> 00:13:32.710
surrounded by scenery that you feel is the most beautiful in the world.

00:13:33.820 --> 00:13:36.460
Until that day, I'll become like wind or water, and wait.

00:13:37.810 --> 00:13:43.470
But even if you become an old woman

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:47.550
without thinking about my teeth or bones,

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:50.120
that'll be fine too.

00:13:58.780 --> 00:13:59.890
Manager...

00:14:01.180 --> 00:14:02.990
<i>You're not the princess in the pages of a book.</i>

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:05.450
<i>You're the real thing.</i>

00:14:07.050 --> 00:14:08.430
I'm so glad you're okay.

00:14:10.540 --> 00:14:13.500
I came back...

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:16.660
I'm sorry.

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:19.920
Why are you apologizing?

00:14:20.740 --> 00:14:21.590
In the end,

00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:25.970
lending my body to your husband

00:14:27.530 --> 00:14:33.280
only made it tougher on both of you.

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:36.610
It might've been a mistake in the first place.

00:14:37.550 --> 00:14:38.890
Hazuki...

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:39.390
I'm sorry.

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:40.430
Hazuki!

00:14:43.900 --> 00:14:44.780
Thank you.

00:14:47.810 --> 00:14:50.270
I never realized.

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:53.790
He was all alone,

00:14:54.570 --> 00:14:56.040
but you found him.

00:14:57.360 --> 00:14:58.550
On top of that,

00:14:59.490 --> 00:15:01.640
you told me about that with all your might, Hazuki,

00:15:03.050 --> 00:15:05.870
and put your life on the line.

00:15:08.310 --> 00:15:10.510
I'm so glad you were here, Hazuki.

00:15:12.210 --> 00:15:13.250
I'm glad

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:17.930
the only one I've ever fallen in love with besides him...

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:22.320
is you,

00:15:25.030 --> 00:15:26.530
Hazuki.

00:15:33.890 --> 00:15:37.500
Just before coming back here,

00:15:38.320 --> 00:15:42.120
I was coloring flowers in front of a rose hedge.

00:15:42.720 --> 00:15:44.670
Before that, I met a mermaid,

00:15:45.120 --> 00:15:47.460
and traveled together with Thumbelina.

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:50.270
You had a fairy tale-like dream, huh?

00:15:50.270 --> 00:15:52.070
I was in a storybook world.

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:54.040
And then

00:15:55.360 --> 00:15:57.260
I heard the talk about bones.

00:15:58.380 --> 00:15:59.210
In other words,

00:15:59.980 --> 00:16:01.350
what I wanna say is...

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:02.770
I think

00:16:04.510 --> 00:16:10.230
I'm the only one who could share with you part of his memories, Manager.

00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:12.320
For you,

00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:17.550
that means there isn't anyone but me.

00:16:17.550 --> 00:16:19.080
You understand that, right?

00:16:20.190 --> 00:16:21.470
You're so close.

00:16:22.140 --> 00:16:25.710
That's because I plan to do this.

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:33.690
And speaking of plans,

00:16:33.690 --> 00:16:36.280
when will you start thinking about remarriage?

00:16:36.280 --> 00:16:37.840
My schedule's free.

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:40.410
This is way too sudden.

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:43.610
No, after being taken down that roundabout route on my own,

00:16:43.610 --> 00:16:45.180
if anything, it's late.

00:16:48.640 --> 00:16:52.710
<i>He better disappear quietly!</i>

00:16:53.850 --> 00:16:55.080
Anyway, I...

00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:55.970
Yes?

00:16:56.640 --> 00:17:01.410
With your permission, Manager, we can eat your husband's bones together.

00:17:05.630 --> 00:17:08.150
If it's a matter of ethics,

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:11.440
we can just lick it together to sample it.

00:17:12.310 --> 00:17:14.380
That wouldn't be a big deal.

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:18.810
See, from now on, I'm going to take up all your time, Manager.

00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:20.810
You're so sure of yourself.

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:22.720
<i>After all,</i>

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:27.190
<i>I've got the healthy manager right in front of me, living and breathing.</i>

00:17:28.750 --> 00:17:30.620
<i>It's fun to feel your heat.</i>

00:17:31.940 --> 00:17:35.630
<i>Until I die, I'll live through this miracle.</i>

00:17:37.300 --> 00:17:42.590
For the longest time, I was in a daze in a strange, dreamlike place.

00:17:44.790 --> 00:17:48.920
But this is even more like a dream and I feel like I'm on cloud nine.

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:53.060
I love you.

00:17:56.540 --> 00:18:00.270
<i>I want to make Rokka happy.</i>

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:16.280
It's like he followed Rokka into death.

00:18:16.800 --> 00:18:19.140
65 years old...

00:18:19.140 --> 00:18:21.290
It was a little soon for your dad, huh?

00:18:21.830 --> 00:18:23.120
I don't know.

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:27.820
Those two were close enough to make you jealous, right?

00:18:27.820 --> 00:18:30.290
All those flowers they gave each other as presents.

00:18:30.870 --> 00:18:35.300
I think Dad would've been happy with anything as long as he lived longer than Mom.

00:18:35.660 --> 00:18:39.100
He was puttering in the garden the day before he passed.

00:18:39.100 --> 00:18:41.100
He was happy in his way.

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:44.790
And my husband said he'd take over the shop.

00:18:44.790 --> 00:18:46.560
I don't think he had any regrets.

00:18:46.920 --> 00:18:49.990
And he lived long enough to see his grandchild, too, right?

00:18:49.990 --> 00:18:52.070
Are you going to move here, Yuki?

00:18:54.180 --> 00:18:55.570
We may just commute from where we live now.

00:18:55.870 --> 00:18:57.250
The place <i>is</i> old...

00:18:57.250 --> 00:18:59.680
That, and... Aunt Miho, do you know about...

00:18:59.680 --> 00:19:00.490
What?

00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:02.950
There's a room that was never to be opened.

00:19:04.600 --> 00:19:07.210
Ever since I was a kid.

00:19:07.210 --> 00:19:11.320
I've got to go in there now to clean it, but I'm kind of scared.

00:19:13.550 --> 00:19:14.660
What are you doing?

00:19:16.450 --> 00:19:18.560
Unlike your mother,

00:19:18.560 --> 00:19:20.220
you resemble your grandmother a lot.

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:21.970
Do you work at the store?

00:19:23.590 --> 00:19:25.220
Yeah. That's right.

00:19:29.180 --> 00:19:30.800
You're going in without knocking?

00:19:33.740 --> 00:19:35.260
Good boy.

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:38.490
Then I'll invite you into my room.

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:53.830
Just kidding.

00:20:01.740 --> 00:20:04.770
I'm banking on not too much surprise on your part,

00:20:05.320 --> 00:20:06.840
so I've got two favors to ask.

00:20:08.650 --> 00:20:13.130
The first is that I want you to dispose of everything in this room.

00:20:13.130 --> 00:20:14.160
Dispose of?

00:20:14.160 --> 00:20:16.960
I mean throw everything away.

00:20:16.960 --> 00:20:17.820
Why?

00:20:18.600 --> 00:20:20.670
This place was taken care of too much.

00:20:21.580 --> 00:20:25.790
But I really don't need it anymore,

00:20:26.660 --> 00:20:28.000
so anytime would be okay.

00:20:28.000 --> 00:20:29.580
If you'd just remember that...

00:20:31.780 --> 00:20:33.200
And the other thing.

00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:33.840
Yeah?

00:20:34.410 --> 00:20:37.210
Would you call me "Grandpa" once?

00:20:40.860 --> 00:20:43.390
My grandpa passed away.

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:25.340
Inside the dreams I always have

00:21:26.460 --> 00:21:31.090
you always smile

00:21:31.090 --> 00:21:35.180
Tell me why

00:21:35.180 --> 00:21:39.060
it won't go away

00:21:39.060 --> 00:21:40.850
I gave you everything

00:21:40.850 --> 00:21:42.690
You gave me anything

00:21:42.690 --> 00:21:47.480
Forever and ever
You're everything,

00:21:47.480 --> 00:21:49.150
still my everything

00:21:49.150 --> 00:21:52.360
I love you

00:21:52.360 --> 00:21:55.740
It is a miracle

00:21:55.740 --> 00:21:58.870
like fleeting snow

00:21:58.870 --> 00:22:04.830
that fell in summer

00:22:05.960 --> 00:22:11.840
If I hadn't met you

00:22:11.840 --> 00:22:15.050
I wouldn't have felt this sadness

00:22:15.050 --> 00:22:22.560
and nothing would have pressed down on my chest

00:22:22.560 --> 00:22:28.230
If I hadn't been able to meet you

00:22:28.230 --> 00:22:35.280
I would never have known the tenderness in strength

00:22:35.280 --> 00:22:40.410
When I close my eyes

00:22:40.410 --> 00:22:44.420
you're right beside me
